a masked mob has attacked teachers and  students of an elite University in New  Delhi the incident is the latest in a  series of violent clashes across India  until Bora has sent us this update from  the jawaharlal nehru campus the  policemen are present here in numbers  today but on Sunday evening when some of  the students and teachers here were  under attack they took their time to  enter the university one must also get  clearance from the security guards so  the students who were beaten up are  asking well the security guards just  careless or was the administration of  the university complicit in the attack  that took place on Sunday evening about  50 people including women wearing masks  holding iron rods in their hands went  from one also to another they beat up  students as well as some teachers and  threatened the students as well at the  moment about 20 people students and some  teachers are receiving treatment at a  hospital in New Delhi now the students  who were beaten up allege that the group  that beat them up weren't gangsters but  part of the ABVP which is a student's  union affiliated with the hindu  nationalist party Janata Party the Home  Minister of the country who comes from  that party has ordered an inquiry and  several ministers in the current  government who've started in this  university have condemned the violence  but the students here don't feel safe  anymore many of them have left their  hostels and gone back home or to their  friends houses to stay there the big  question that people are now asking is  because there's a sense of disbelief and  panic then how could such an attack take  place our students now not safe inside  their hostels the students of this  university have been protesting against  the controversial citizenship law and  more recently also against the proposed  fee hike
 

